    Forked from mage-os/module-rma 2.4.1 into Magenx_Rma / Magenx_RmaGraphQl;
    identifiers renamed, GraphQL surface split into a sibling module.

    New-RMA e-mails hang off rma_commit_after, which RmaSubmitService::createRma()
    dispatches once its transaction has committed — i.e. the customer-initiated
    (GraphQL) create-return flow. This is deliberate: RMAs opened by an admin from
    Sales > RMA, or through POST /V1/rma, do NOT notify the customer or the admin
    recipient, because those paths save through RMARepository directly.

    RMARepository also dispatches rma_created_after on every insert, and nothing in
    this module subscribes to it. That is intentional too — it is left as the
    extension point for integrations that DO want to observe every creation path.
    Subscribing SendNewRmaEmails to it as well would make the GraphQL flow fire
    both events and send twice.
-->
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:Event/etc/events.xsd">
    <event name="rma_commit_after">
        <observer name="magenx_rma_send_new_rma_emails" instance="Magenx\Rma\Observer\SendNewRmaEmails"/>
    </event>
    <event name="rma_status_change_after">
        <observer name="magenx_rma_send_status_change_email" instance="Magenx\Rma\Observer\SendStatusChangeEmail"/>
    </event>
</config>
